# interpretation / caveats
if 'Q15 round' not in r['interpretation']:
    r['interpretation']+=" [Q15 round] The red-shifted dense-gas ridge ~3.3\" N of S (coincident with Michiyama+2018 OF-Red) is real in HCN 3-2 (5.9 sigma pointwise, recovered in Xb4b and in the baseline-free tapered cube) and tentative in HCO+; its origin (S counter-lobe vs Bridge/N-related) is undecided: symmetric wing velocity and flux and the OF-Red coincidence favour a counter-lobe, while the N/Bridge-like core velocity and the continuous red tongue to N favour an inter-nuclear/N association. Bipolarity of the dense S outflow is permitted, not established."
cav="Q15: (a) the red-side baseline is an extrapolation (all line-free channels are blue of the line), giving +-40% on the HCN ridge flux and 2-4 sigma on HCO+; (b) significance is pointwise at an a-priori position (team-b p0017, M18) and the red-window noise is non-Gaussian; (c) no CO or low-J HCN/HCO+ at <=1\" in the archive, so kinematic discrimination of counter-lobe vs Bridge/N streaming is not possible with ratios (HCN/HCO+ 3.3+-1.8 vs 2.0+-0.7) or the p-v alone; (d) Xb47 4-3 is blended at 4.5\" and baseline-limited; (e) fluxes are 1.05\" beam aperture values from uncleaned channels (Q13e), i.e. lower limits for extended emission; (f) dynamical times are projected with no inclination correction."
if isinstance(r['caveats'],list):
    r['caveats']=[c for c in r['caveats'] if not c.startswith('Q15:')]+[cav]
# fix invalid confidence enums
for x in r['results']:
    if x['confidence'] not in ('high','medium','low','tentative'):
        x['confidence']={'medium-low':'low'}.get(x['confidence'],'low')
json.dump(r,open(p,'w'),indent=1); print(len(r['results']))
